# Release signing for the Android TV app. Copy to
# `~/.android/tinytrack.keystore.properties` and point it at your copy of the
# upload keystore — a PER-MACHINE file, beside the .jks it names, which is what
# lets every worktree of this tree sign alike. (`keystore.properties` in this
# directory, the shell's Gradle root, still wins where it exists: that is what
# the release workflow writes on a runner, and what a one-off override should do.
# It is gitignored, so it reaches one checkout and no other.) NEVER commit either
# file or the .jks.
#
# The upload key already exists (alias tinytrack-tv). Do NOT generate a new one:
# Play accepts only the signature the app was first published with, so a fresh
# key locks you out of updating it. Keep the .jks and these passwords backed up
# somewhere that is not this machine, for exactly that reason.
#
# These values must match the ANDROID_KEYSTORE_* / ANDROID_KEY_* secrets that
# .github/workflows/release.yml writes into this same file on a runner, or a
# local build and a CI build ship artifacts Play sees as two different apps.
#
# storeFile must be an ABSOLUTE path, so the .jks can live outside the repo.
#
# keytool -genkeypair writes PKCS12, which carries ONE password for the store and
# its entries, so keyPassword is the store password again rather than a second
# secret. Set it explicitly here and in the CI secret; an empty value is not read
# as "the store's".
storeFile=/absolute/path/to/tinytrack.keystore.jks
storePassword=CHANGEME
keyAlias=tinytrack-tv
keyPassword=CHANGEME
